# 2778. Sum of Squares of Special Elements

### Problem
Given an integer array `nums` of length `n`, an element is considered special if its 1-based index divides `n` evenly. Calculate and return the sum of squares of all special elements.

### Approach
- Find the size `n` of the array and initialize `sum = 0`.
- Traverse the array using a loop from index `0` to `n-1`.
- Check whether `n` is divisible by the 1-based index `i + 1`.
- If divisible, add the square of `nums[i]` to `sum`.
- Return the final sum.

### Code
```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int sumOfSquares(vector<int>& nums) {
        int n = nums.size();
        int sum = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if (n % (i + 1) == 0) {
                sum += nums[i] * nums[i];
            }
        }

        return sum;
    }
};
```
